description:
Sprint-18 spec-review adjacent finding (2026-10-06, pre-existing DATA LOSS, out of f9b9 scope): `doctor --fix` DELETES fresh records with an unregistered type (e.g. "wtf") — ours maps doctor_detail(schema-invalid)->Invalid and removes them ("Removed 1 invalid record(s)"), the reference KEEPS unknown-type records explicitly (doctor.ts applyFixes case schema-validation: `const valid = records.filter((r) => !registry.get(r.type) || validate(r))` with the comment "Keep unknown-type records — they're flagged separately by checkUnknownTypes and shouldn't be silently deleted"). Probe: store with one type-wtf record; reference --fix leaves it, ours empties the file. FIX: apply_fixes must treat unknown-type records as Keep (the unknown-types check reports them separately; it is NOT fixable in the reference either). Pin differentially: fresh unknown-type record survives --fix in both, no Removed line, store byte-equal.

ARCH GATE @18 UPGRADE (2026-10-07, candidate C5, TOP PICK — bug-first: data loss before architecture): the fix is not a local keep-unknown patch; align apply_fixes to the REFERENCE CASE SEQUENCE per domain (doctor.ts applyFixes order):
(1) schema-validation pass: malformed + schema-invalid records -> Removed; unknown-type records -> KEEP (the d45c data loss; checkUnknownTypes flags them separately, never silently deleted);
(2) stale pass over the REMAINDER -> Pruned (fixes the stale+invalid precedence from mulch-f7ec: a record both stale and invalid reports Removed, because the reference applies cases in CHECK order — schema-validation rewrites the file first, the stale case prunes the remainder);
(3) legacy outcome migration on survivors (singular outcome -> outcomes[], with the reference "Migrated N legacy ..." report line — the 0c47 remainder).
Report stays check-ordered: all Removed lines, then all Pruned, then Migrated. Typeless stale detail renders `stale undefined` (JS stringify of the missing type; f7ec finding 1). Absorbs mulch-f7ec (closed superseded); closes mulch-0c47 (split delivered via read_lenient + Check catalog; only repair semantics remained). mulch-3368 (failure_envelope) free-rides if touched. Pin differentially: pathological stores (unknown-type fresh/stale, stale+invalid overlap, legacy singular outcome, typeless records).
